From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:12:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Rules 5: committees only from verifiers that declared the
 job's model

With several models' pools open (testnet Rules 4), DrawCommittee seated any staker on any job:
verifiers holding only Qwen3 were drawn for Llama and Mistral jobs, could not compute them, paid
the no-show penalty, and 7 wrong Llama jobs settled with no verifier able to check them.

VERIFIER_MODELS (op 24): an account declares up to 16 registered models it verifies (strictly
increasing ids; empty withdraws). From Rules 5:
- a staker is drawn for a job only if it declared the job's model;
- JOB_ACCEPT and POOL_CLAIM fail unless a staked verifier of the model exists;
- a committed job for which no committee can be drawn (its verifiers left after the claim) is
  aborted with the fee (a pool unit's verification pay, back to its category) and bond returned.
Before Rules 5 the op fails and everything behaves as in Rules 4. Declarations are committed in
the state root under 'v' (no entries before Rules 5, so old roots are unchanged).

RPC: getjobstate adds verifiers (model -> staked verifiers that declared it), getjobaccount adds
models. uwcctl verifiermodels <key> [model ...]. Not scheduled on any network yet.

